/*
 * Failure-injection fixture for tests/patient_dropped.nf.test — "one patient's task is
 * dropped by errorStrategy 'ignore', partway through the patient list".
 *
 * THE FAILURE MODE THIS REPRODUCES. `conf/modules.config` gives seven QC processes an
 * errorStrategy whose fallthrough branch is `'ignore'`: a task that fails the wrong way
 * is DROPPED and the run keeps going, exit 0. Every per-patient fan-in in this pipeline
 * was a plain `Channel.join()` — `failOnMismatch`/`failOnDuplicate` appeared NOWHERE in
 * the repo — so one ignored task on one patient removed that patient from the five-join
 * checkpoint chain silently, and `csv/postprocessed.csv` came out one row short with
 * nothing anywhere saying so. The short CSV is then read back by the next `--start`, and
 * the patient is simply gone: half-published and invisible.
 *
 * WHY THIS FIXTURE PINS THE STRATEGY EXPLICITLY, unlike
 * tests/testdata/failing_p002_registration.config next to it. That fixture deliberately
 * injects NO errorStrategy, because the property it pins (an orderly shutdown still
 * flushes the completed patients' rows) has to be the one a real run would see. This one
 * is the opposite case: the whole point is the `'ignore'` branch, and MERGE_AND_PYRAMID
 * is not one of the seven processes `conf/modules.config` puts on it. So the strategy is
 * stated here — the fixture is "what happens when a checkpoint-chain producer IS ignored",
 * which is a configuration this repo already ships for seven of its processes and which a
 * site profile, a future `withName:` selector or one more QC process can extend to an
 * eighth at any time.
 *
 * MERGE_AND_PYRAMID is chosen because `pyramid` is the LAST field of the postprocessed
 * checkpoint chain: every other artifact for P002 is produced, published, and paid for
 * before the drop, which is exactly the shape that made the loss expensive and invisible.
 */

process {
    withName: 'MERGE_AND_PYRAMID' {
        errorStrategy = 'ignore'
        beforeScript  = { task.tag != 'P002' ? 'true' : """
echo "forced P002 pyramid failure, swallowed by errorStrategy 'ignore'" >&2
exit 1
""" }
    }
}
